

⭐ Blueprint Panel — Full Specification

This panel has three major zones, each with a different purpose:

Blueprint Source View — the DSL code that generated the scene

Runtime Blueprint State — the active model, meta‑equation, and parameters

Frame‑Aligned Metadata — values for Θ, Ξ, organisms, and observers at the current frame

Each zone is collapsible and independently scrollable.

🔶 1. Blueprint Source View

This shows the exact DSL snippet that produced the cinematic output.

Features:

Syntax‑highlighted CMB‑Blueprint code

Auto‑scroll to the active block (model, organism, meta‑equation)

Click‑to‑jump: clicking a code block highlights the corresponding region in the viewport

Version tag (commit hash if loaded from GitHub)

Example structure:

universe "CMB-Time-Weave" {
  grid { dimensions: 3; resolution: [128,128,128]; }

  fields {
    time_field Θ: scalar;
    meta_model Ξ: enum { CLASSICAL, WARP };
  }

  models {
    WARP { use: WarpTimeModel; }
  }

  meta_equation {
    use: DefaultMetaEquation;
  }
}

Controls:

Copy

Collapse/Expand

Highlight active section

Show diff (if multiple versions loaded)

This zone gives you authorship visibility — your blueprint is always visible.

